{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["רב — 'Enough for my recovering heart that I did not believe otherwise, but surely Joseph my son is still alive.' They say [it is] the peshat of others [that it means] with cunning, and these are nonsense. And I, the younger one, heard: רב — 'Joseph my son is still alive.' You say:" "עוד יוסף חי — If he is ruling, רב לי, it is enough for me that he is still alive even if he is not ruling. אלכה ואראנו בטרם אמות — 'I will go and see him before I die,' and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The text as transmitted appears internally garbled: the opening explanation of רב is quoted as if from another source, followed by a dismissal of 'others' and then a first-person alternative. Rendered hyper-literally; sense is uncertain.", 1 "The lemma עוד יוסף חי differs from the Masoretic text of Gen 45:28, which reads עוד־יוסף בני חי; rendered exactly as the lemma appears in Rashbam's text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:22.406687278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}